    "created_at": "2016-10-04T01:57:45Z",
    "updated_at": "2016-10-04T01:57:45Z",
    "body": "Text inside buttons and select boxes is selectable in Chrome and Edge (I don't have Safari to test with).\n\nTo me, this back-and-forth underscores my point: the spec should not be placing restrictions on browser UI choices like this. Firefox wants to enforce a UI where web pages act more like native apps, and that's fine. Other browsers have chosen not go that route. That should be a product decision, not a spec decision.\n",
    "author_association": "MEMBER",
    "pin": null,
    "reactions": {
